  "details": "I program games. I would like to make a game and upload it to VRChat to play with my friends. I know there is a high security risk involved with allowing custom script. \n\nI propose the ability to upload a world with custom scripts but not allow portals to be dropped for high risk map. \n\nTo do this you would first have to detect any custom scripts (which happens on upload) and flag the map as high risk. (requires an extra bit in the database) Then disable dropping portals for that specific map (you do this when there is a player nearby or when too close to spawn.) You would also have an \"OPT-IN to view custom script maps\" checkbox in system settings.\n\nThen in the meantime you can work on the halting problem of making sure that custom scripts don't hijack users computer and download their credit card information from their browser's caching systems.\n\nAlternatively if you would don't want to have to detect for custom scripts you could build a checkbox on the upload UI. Allowing the creator to flag a custom script map.",
